## Step 0 — baseline, voice VLAN NOT configured (13:08:10–13:08:47) — evidence/38410/38410-s0.out, -s0-phone.pcap
The phone sent 34 LLDPDUs over 35 s. The DUT answered with 4 LLDPDUs (a fast-start burst of 3 at 1 s
intervals, then one at +30 s), each carrying port-id port3.0.13, MED Capabilities `0027` + device
type `04` (network connectivity), and **no Network Policy TLV**:
```
rx LLDPDU from 02:00:cd:37:0d:6f: [('port-id', 'port3.0.13'), ..., ('MED-capabilities', '002704')]
voice network policy: None
```

## Step 1 + 2 — configuration (u5, 13:09:08–13:09:32, ckcon --stop-on-error, no `% ` line) — evidence/38410/38410-cfg-u5.out
```
configure terminal
vlan database / vlan 3997 name ck-voice / exit
interface port3.0.13 / switchport voice vlan 3997 / exit
service dhcp-server
interface vlan3997 / ip address 192.168.97.1/24 / exit
ip dhcp pool ck-voice / network 192.168.97.0/24 / range 192.168.97.100 192.168.97.150 / default-router 192.168.97.1 / lease 0 1 0 / exit
end
```
Read back:
- `show running-config interface port3.0.13` → switchport mode access / **spanning-tree portfast**
  (added by the voice-vlan command, as the AW+ page says) / switchport voice vlan 3997;
- `show vlan 3997` → ck-voice STATIC ACTIVE port3.0.13(t) (the access port became a TAGGED member of
  the voice VLAN on its own);
- `show ip dhcp pool` → ck-voice 192.168.97.0/24, 100–150, lease 0:1:0:0, default-router
  192.168.97.1, 51 dynamic, 0 leased;
- `show ip interface brief` → vlan3997 192.168.97.1/24 running.

## Step 3 — the phone connects (13:10:36–13:11:21) — evidence/38410/38410-s2.out, -s2-phone.pcap, -s2-eth1.pcap (tcpdump), -s2-dut.out
(Run s1, 13:09:56, had only an 8 s LLDP window, and no DUT LLDPDU fell inside it: the phone was
already a known neighbour, so there was no new fast-start burst, and the periodic interval is 30 s.
The DUT's `show lldp neighbors detail` at 13:10:18 listed port3.0.13 → `ck-phone`, Telephone,
`LLDP-MED Device Type: Endpoint Class III`. s2 re-ran it with a 40 s window.)

Network policy advertised by the DUT (decoded by phone.py and, independently, by tcpdump -v):
```
13:10:44.255 02:00:cd:37:0d:6f > 01:80:c2:00:00:0e LLDP
	Organization specific TLV (127), length 8: OUI ANSI/TIA (0x0012bb)
	  Network policy Subtype (2)
	    Application type [voice] (0x01), Flags [Tagged]
	    Vlan id 3997, L2 priority 5, DSCP value 0
13:11:14.535  (same TLV again, 30 s later)
```
DHCP in the advertised VLAN (the phone tagged VID 3997, PCP 5, broadcast flag set):
```
13:11:17.698 00:00:5e:00:53:10 > ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff vlan 3997, p 5  DHCP Discover
13:11:17.70–18.54  00:00:cd:37:0d:6f vlan 3997  ARP who-has 192.168.97.100 tell 192.168.97.1  x5   (the pool's ping/ARP conflict probe)
13:11:18.751 00:00:cd:37:0d:6f > ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff vlan 3997, p 0  192.168.97.1.67 > 255.255.255.255.68 DHCP Reply (OFFER)
13:11:18.962 phone vlan 3997, p 5  DHCP Request
13:11:19.033 DUT vlan 3997  DHCP Reply (ACK)
phone.py:  OFFER from 00:00:cd:37:0d:6f (192.168.97.1) vlan=3997: yiaddr=192.168.97.100 server_id=192.168.97.1 router=192.168.97.1 lease=3600
           ACK   from 00:00:cd:37:0d:6f vlan=3997: yiaddr=192.168.97.100 router=192.168.97.1 lease=3600 mask=255.255.255.0
           ARP reply: 192.168.97.1 is-at 00:00:cd:37:0d:6f vlan=3997
           ICMP echo replies: 3/3, vlan=[3997]
```
DUT view (13:11:26–13:11:30):
```
show ip dhcp binding  -> 192.168.97.100  0000.5e00.5310  Dynamic  30 Sep 2026 01:12:01 (UTC)
show mac address-table | include 0000.5e00.5310
   1    port3.0.13   0000.5e00.5310   forward  dynamic   (its untagged LLDP)
   3997 port3.0.13   0000.5e00.5310   forward  dynamic   (its tagged voice traffic)
show counter dhcp-server -> DISCOVER in 1, REQUEST in 1, OFFER out 1, ACK out 1, NAK 0
```
Not graded, noted:
- the DUT sends its own frames in the voice VLAN at PCP 0 (the advertised priority 5 is for the phone);
- `show arp` did not list 192.168.97.100 (the emulator does not answer the DUT's later ARP
  requests; the ICMP replies went to the requesting MAC).

